<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lajos Kossuth</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1802–1894</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lajos Kossuth was a Hungarian lawyer, journalist and statesman, the leading figure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungarian-revolution-of-1848">Hungarian Revolution of 1848</a>. As finance minister and head of the National Defence Committee he organised resistance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, and after the Declaration of Independence of April 1849 he was elected governor-president. After defeat by Austrian and Russian armies he went into exile, where he died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lajos-kossuth.jpg" alt="Lajos Kossuth" width="320" height="449" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Southworth &amp;amp; Hawes · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Lajos_Kossuth,_1852.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
